  "page_date": "",
  "chunk_title": "Deploy a fine-tuned model",
  "chunk_content": "Deploy a fine-tuned model  Once your model is fine-tuned, you can deploy the model and can use it in your own application. You can't deploy a fine-tuned model from the deployments page or the playground page in Azure AI Studio. The only way, currently, to deploy a fine-tuned model is from the model details page for that model.  When you deploy the model, you make the model available for inferencing, and that incurs an hourly hosting charge. Fine-tuned models, however, can be stored in Azure AI Studio at no cost until you're ready to use them.  [!INCLUDE Fine-tuning deletion]  > [!NOTE] > Only one deployment is permitted for a fine-tuned model. An error message is displayed if you select an already-deployed fine-tuned model.  You can monitor the progress of your deployment on the Deployments page in Azure AI Studio.",
